# pagination.zd — one page of a long list at a time.
#
# `page` is the caller's `Whole` signal, counted from zero because
# `indices` and `listTake`/`listDrop` are; the numbers a reader sees are
# `page + 1`, converted in one place here rather than at every use site.
#
# THE DECISION WORTH NAMING: Previous on the first page is present and
# announced unavailable, rather than absent.
#
# This file used to render no button there at all, and said why: the
# closed argument set had no `disabled`, only a `disabled` *style prefix*
# for colouring a control disabled by some other means, so the choice was
# between a control that vanishes and a live one that silently does
# nothing. A tab stop leading nowhere is worse than a missing control, so
# the control went missing.
#
# `disabled is yes` reaches `aria-disabled`, which is the third answer and
# the right one. The button stays in the document and in the tab order, a
# reader who arrives at it is told it is unavailable instead of finding
# nothing there, the row does not reflow as you page, and the branch that
# says `disabled` carries no `on click` — so it is inert because it has no
# behaviour, not because something suppressed one.
#
# It is *not* HTML's `disabled`, which would take the control out of the
# tab order and take its announcement with it. That attribute is still not
# in the vocabulary, and `elements.rs` says why.

component Pagination with page, count, class, pageClass, currentClass
    Navigation class is class, label is "Pagination"
        Row
            if page > 0
                Button "Previous", class is pageClass
                    on click
                        subtract 1 from page
            otherwise
                Button "Previous", class is pageClass, disabled is yes
            each index in (indices of count)
                PageNumber index, page is page, pageClass is pageClass, currentClass is currentClass
            if page < count - 1
                Button "Next", class is pageClass
                    on click
                        add 1 to page
            otherwise
                Button "Next", class is pageClass, disabled is yes

# The current page is the one entry that is not a button, which is visible
# to everyone; `current is "page"` is what says the same thing to a reader
# who is listening rather than looking.
component PageNumber with index, page, pageClass, currentClass
    if index is page
        Text (index + 1), class is currentClass, current is "page"
    otherwise
        Button (index + 1), class is pageClass
            on click
                set page to index
